Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:46:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: the game's constants and workarounds come from
 its profile (dm/games), plus a coverage survey

horizon_game.py reads dm/games/<id>/game.tsv through game.py (program_id, modules, sys_resource) and an optional linux_profile.py; horizon_run.py has no title table any more; GetInfo reports the profile's program ID. survey.py counts how every function is handled (lifted, replaced by origin, JIT, not translated, with the reason).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: NX2Linux milestone C: no title is written in the runtime; the profile folder decides, and a survey says how each function of a game is handled
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch Téo/jalon-c-profils-survey)

